1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,429
Coach: An invitation can make space for another view.

2
00:00:03,429 --> 00:00:09,857
Coach: It should not turn a quieter moment into a test that someone has to pass.

3
00:00:09,857 --> 00:00:12,429
Coach: Start with what you can observe:

4
00:00:12,429 --> 00:00:15,429
Coach: who has commented on the current question,

5
00:00:15,429 --> 00:00:18,429
Coach: and what contribution would help the discussion.

6
00:00:18,779 --> 00:00:20,922
Coach: This is a fresh excerpt.

7
00:00:20,922 --> 00:00:26,065
Coach: Maya’s paired introductions and Noah’s drawing or writing suggestion are both available,

8
00:00:26,065 --> 00:00:28,208
Coach: but neither has been chosen.

9
00:00:28,208 --> 00:00:31,636
Coach: Maya has not yet commented on their comparison.

10
00:00:31,636 --> 00:00:37,208
Coach: That tells us nothing certain about her reasons or what she privately prefers.

11
00:00:37,558 --> 00:00:39,701
Coach: Keep the task in view.

12
00:00:39,701 --> 00:00:43,558
Coach: The activity should help new members meet one another

13
00:00:43,558 --> 00:00:46,987
Coach: and find out about the weekly drawing group.

14
00:00:46,987 --> 00:00:49,987
Coach: An invitation can ask about that connection,

15
00:00:49,987 --> 00:00:55,987
Coach: rather than demand a complete new plan or ask why someone has been quiet.

16
00:01:04,337 --> 00:01:07,337
Coach: You could offer the question to everyone,

17
00:01:07,337 --> 00:01:11,194
Coach: or invite Maya if there is a natural opening.

18
00:01:11,194 --> 00:01:16,765
Coach: Keep it narrow enough to answer, and leave a genuine option to pass.

19
00:01:16,765 --> 00:01:23,194
Coach: A polite phrase is not enough if the person is still expected to justify declining.

20
00:01:23,544 --> 00:01:30,830
You: Maya, would you like to add anything about how these ideas could connect to the drawing group?

21
00:01:30,830 --> 00:01:34,687
You: It is fine to pass or come in later.

22
00:01:35,037 --> 00:01:37,537
Maya: I will listen for now.

23
00:01:37,887 --> 00:01:40,387
You: Of course.

24
00:01:40,737 --> 00:01:43,737
Coach: The invitation has been declined for now.

25
00:01:43,737 --> 00:01:47,166
Coach: Accept that response and return to the subject.

26
00:01:47,166 --> 00:01:51,880
Coach: Do not ask for a reason, announce that Maya lacks confidence,

27
00:01:51,880 --> 00:01:55,737
Coach: or treat her choice as agreement with either activity.

28
00:01:55,737 --> 00:01:58,737
Coach: She can decide whether to contribute later.

29
00:01:59,087 --> 00:02:03,373
Coach: An invitation can also hide an attempt to obtain approval.

30
00:02:03,373 --> 00:02:08,944
Coach: Maya, you agree with me, right, points toward the answer the speaker wants.

31
00:02:08,944 --> 00:02:14,516
Coach: Asking what she would add or question leaves room for a different view.

32
00:02:14,516 --> 00:02:18,373
Coach: The distinction is about the choice you actually offer.

33
00:02:18,723 --> 00:02:23,866
Coach: Do not keep returning to the same person after they have passed.

34
00:02:23,866 --> 00:02:29,437
Coach: Give space to the discussion and attend to a later attempt to join.

35
00:02:29,437 --> 00:02:33,723
Coach: Supporting participation includes making room when someone offers a point,

36
00:02:33,723 --> 00:02:36,723
Coach: not merely choosing who should speak next.

37
00:02:37,073 --> 00:02:41,787
Coach: Equal speaking time is not a rule for every group discussion.

38
00:02:41,787 --> 00:02:44,787
Coach: Someone might make a brief useful observation;

39
00:02:44,787 --> 00:02:46,930
Coach: another point may need explanation.

40
00:02:46,930 --> 00:02:51,216
Coach: Stay attentive to access and relevance without counting compulsory turns

41
00:02:51,216 --> 00:02:54,216
Coach: or taking authority to allocate everyone’s words.

42
00:02:54,566 --> 00:02:58,423
Coach: Return to the comparison before any invitation was made.

43
00:02:58,423 --> 00:03:03,995
Coach: Privately form a brief invitation that relates to the task and allows passing.

44
00:03:03,995 --> 00:03:07,852
Coach: You could address the group rather than one person.

45
00:03:07,852 --> 00:03:13,852
Coach: Do not rehearse another request after Maya has already said she wants to listen.

46
00:03:26,202 --> 00:03:31,345
Coach: Check what your wording asks for and whether declining is genuinely possible.

47
00:03:31,345 --> 00:03:36,916
Coach: After an invitation, leave room for an answer, a pass, or continued thinking.

48
00:03:36,916 --> 00:03:43,773
Coach: The aim is an opening the person can use, not a promise that they will speak.
